1. ORDER BY (Sabse Simple)
Matlab:
Result ko sort (arrange) karna — chhote se bade ya bade se chhote order mein.
Kab use karte hain?
Jab tumhe data ascending (A to Z / chhota se bada) ya descending (Z to A / bada se chhota) mein chahiye.
Syntax:

SQLSELECT column1, column2
FROM table_name
ORDER BY column_name ASC/DESC;

SELECT prd_key, prd_nm, prd_cost
FROM bronze.crm_prd_info
ORDER BY prd_cost ASC;     -- ASC = Ascending (chhota pehle)



2. Group BY

Matlab:
Rows ko groups mein baantna jinke same values hain.
Kab use karte hain?
Jab tumhe aggregate (summary) chahiye jaise:

Kitne customers male hain?
Har product ki total sales kitni hai?
Har city mein kitne customers hain?

Important Rule:
GROUP BY ke saath aggregate functions use karte hain jaise:

COUNT()
SUM()
AVG()
MIN()

SELECT column1, aggregate_function(column2)
FROM table_name
GROUP BY column1;

SELECT 
    cst_gndr,
    COUNT(*) AS total_customers
FROM bronze.crm_cust_info
GROUP BY cst_gndr;


SELECT 
    cst_gndr,
    cst_marital_status,
    COUNT(*) AS total_customers
FROM bronze.crm_cust_info
GROUP BY cst_gndr, cst_marital_status;   -- ✅ Sahi (dono columns GROUP BY mein)

Rule Samjho (Golden Rule of GROUP BY)
Rule:
SELECT mein jo bhi non-aggregate columns hain (matlab jo aggregate function ke saath nahi hain), un sabko GROUP BY mein daalna padega.


